APLAN008 resolves `traces` anchors against the repo root by default. It used to
default to *off*, so `check` printed `ok` while silently skipping one of the ten
invariants it advertises.

```
$ aplan check
? 1
error[APLAN008] F-002: `traces` target `NOPE.md` does not exist
  --> aplan/tasks/F-002.md:7:1
  fix: Create `NOPE.md` or correct the trace path.
failed: 1 error(s), 0 warning(s) across 2 tasks

```

Skipping the check is now something you ask for, not something that happens to
you.

```
$ aplan check --no-traces
ok: 2 tasks, 0 warning(s), DAG acyclic

```
